The Security Council,

Reaffirming the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations,

Recalling all its relevant resolutions on the situation in the Middle East, including the Palestinian question, in particular resolutions 2712 (2023), 2720 (2023), 2728 (2024), and 2735 (2024),

Reaffirming its primary responsibility under the Charter of the United Nations for the maintenance of international peace and security,

Expressing grave concern over the ongoing catastrophic humanitarian situation in the Gaza Strip, including the acute lack of access to basic services and humanitarian assistance, the severe risk of famine, particularly in northern Gaza, and the unprecedented civilian suffering and displacement,

Emphasizing that international humanitarian law must be respected under all circumstances, including the prohibition of starvation of civilians as a method of warfare, and recalling that the civilian population and civilian objects, including hospitals, schools, and humanitarian facilities, must be respected and protected,

Reiterating its deep appreciation for the indispensable and vital role of the United Nations and its agencies, particularly the United Nations Relief and Works Agency for Palestine Refugees in the Near East (UNRWA), as the backbone of the humanitarian response in Gaza,

1. Demands an immediate, unconditional and permanent ceasefire to be respected by all parties; and further reiterates its demand for the immediate and unconditional release of all hostages;

2. Demands immediate access by the civilian population in the Gaza Strip to basic services and humanitarian assistance indispensable to its survival, and rejects any effort to starve Palestinians;

3. Calls further for the immediate, safe, unhindered and massive delivery of humanitarian assistance at scale throughout the entire Gaza Strip, including to the besieged northern governorates, and for the removal of all obstacles to the provision of such assistance;

4. Demands that the parties fully comply with their obligations under international law, including international humanitarian law and international human rights law, notably in relation to the protection of civilians, in particular women and children, and persons hors de combat, as well as the protection of civilian and humanitarian infrastructure;

5. Underlines that UNRWA remains the backbone of the humanitarian response in Gaza and calls upon all parties to enable the Agency to carry out its mandate as adopted by the General Assembly in all its areas of operations;

6. Urges all parties to fully implement resolution 2735 (2024) without delay;

7. Requests the Secretary-General to report to the Security Council on the implementation of this resolution within three weeks of its adoption;

8. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

